# HD2D Unity workflow

Keep the Unity Editor open on this project (`C:\Users\User\Documents\Unity\HD2D`).

## Use Unity (MCP / `unity command`) for Editor-owned data

Scenes, prefabs, GameObjects, components, transforms, import settings, materials, packages, play mode, console, hierarchy.

Never hand-edit `.unity`, `.prefab`, or `.asset` YAML while the Editor is connected.

## Edit C# in the repo

Write gameplay code under `Assets/Scripts`. After new scripts, wait for compile (`recompile` / `recompile_status`) before `attach_script`.

Prefer `unity command` / Unity MCP over guessing scene YAML.

## Layout

- `Assets/Scripts/Runtime` — `KVH.Game` (feature folders: `Player`, `Input`, `Interaction`, `Lighting`, `Camera`, `Flow`, `UI`, …)
- `Assets/Scripts/Editor` — `KVH.Game.Editor`
- `Assets/KylePixelator` — presentation only (`KVH.KylePixelator`)
- `Assets/Docs/Architecture.md` — JRPG deps, UI, naming
- Scenes: `CastleYard` (brick yard explore), `PondLab` (water), `Field` (outdoor grass), `SceneSandbox` (bare prototype), `MovementLab`, `RoomDemo`, `PixelLab` (raw shader lab)
- Art, audio, prefabs, ScriptableObjects in their named folders

If `unity status` is not `ready`, fix the Editor connection before changing scenes.
